#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/server/databases/postgresql.xml:99
#, xml-text
msgid "Installation of PostgreSQL"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/server/databases/postgresql.xml:102
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"For enhanced security, it is better to have a dedicated group and user for "
"running the PostgreSQL server. First, issue as the <systemitem "
"class=\"username\">root</systemitem> user:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/server/databases/postgresql.xml:107
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>groupadd -g 41 postgres &amp;&amp;\n"
"useradd -c \"PostgreSQL Server\" -g postgres -d /srv/pgsql/data \\\n"
"        -u 41 postgres</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/server/databases/postgresql.xml:113
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"There are several configuration items that add additional functionality with"
" optional packages to <application>PostgreSQL</application>.  Use "
"<command>./configure --help</command> to see a list."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/server/databases/postgresql.xml:128
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Install <application>PostgreSQL</application> with the following commands:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/server/databases/postgresql.xml:132
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>sed -e '/DEFAULT_PGSOCKET_DIR/s@/tmp@/run/postgresql@' \\\n"
"    -i src/include/pg_config_manual.h                  &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"./configure --prefix=/usr \\\n"
"            --docdir=/usr/share/doc/postgresql-&postgresql-version; &amp;&amp;\n"
"make</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/server/databases/postgresql.xml:140
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"There are a number of programs in the <filename "
"class=\"directory\">contrib/</filename> directory. If you are going to run "
"this installation as a server and wish to build some of them, enter "
"<command>make -C contrib</command> or <command>make -C "
"contrib/<replaceable>&lt;SUBDIR-NAME&gt;</replaceable></command> for each "
"subdirectory."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/server/databases/postgresql.xml:149
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Tests must be run as an unprivileged user because they need to start a "
"temporary server and this is prevented as the root user. For the same "
"reason, you need to stop all PostgreSQL servers if any are running. If a "
"previous version of PostgreSQL is installed, it may be necessary to use "
"<command>--disable-rpath</command> with <command>configure</command> to "
"avoid failures, but <emphasis>installing the binaries created using this "
"switch is not recommended</emphasis>. To test the results, issue: "
"<command>make check</command>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/server/databases/postgresql.xml:160
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If you are installing <application>PostgreSQL</application> to upgrade an "
"existing installation, there are important steps that you need to follow. If"
" the major version of the new build is greater than the previous version, "
"there is a chance that the data file format has changed.  New software "
"cannot use the existing data files. In this case, the server will not start "
"because the old programs have been overwritten, so the data is unavailable "
"until it's file format has been converted."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/server/databases/postgresql.xml:169
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Before upgrading an existing installation of PostgreSQL, check the "
"documentation for any considerations that you must keep in mind during the "
"upgrade. Note that new major versions might use a different binary format in"
" the data objects, causing potential incompatibilities.  For more "
"information, please review upstream's documentation about upgrading "
"PostgreSQL here: <ulink "
"url=\"https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/upgrading.html\"/>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/server/databases/postgresql.xml:178
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"At this point, you may have both the old and the new binaries installed on "
"your filesystem. These binaries can be used to perform an upgrade of your "
"existing database files. For the following instructions it is assumed that"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><para><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/server/databases/postgresql.xml:183
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"The actual data files are stored in <filename "
"class=\"directory\">/srv/pgsql/data</filename>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><para><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/server/databases/postgresql.xml:186
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"The upgraded data files will be stored in <filename "
"class=\"directory\">/srv/pgsql/newdata</filename>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><para><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/server/databases/postgresql.xml:189
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"There is enough disk space to hold the actual data files twice. The upgrade "
"is not an inline upgrade but it will copy the data to new database files."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/server/databases/postgresql.xml:196
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"First, do a temporary install which makes access to the new binaries much "
"easier:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/server/databases/postgresql.xml:198
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>make DESTDIR=$(pwd)/DESTDIR install</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/server/databases/postgresql.xml:200
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Next, create a directory which is writable by the <systemitem "
"class=\"username\">postgres</systemitem> user, as the <systemitem "
"class=\"username\">root</systemitem> user:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/server/databases/postgresql.xml:204
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>install -d -o postgres $(pwd)/DESTDIR/tmp</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/server/databases/postgresql.xml:206
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Now, stop the existing instance of <application>PostgreSQL</application> and"
" start the upgrade process as the <systemitem "
"class=\"username\">root</systemitem> user:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/server/databases/postgresql.xml:210
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>pushd $(pwd)/DESTDIR/tmp\n"
"/etc/rc.d/init.d/postgresql stop\n"
"su postgres -c \"../usr/bin/initdb -D /srv/pgsql/newdata\"\n"
"su postgres -c \"../usr/bin/pg_upgrade \\\n"
"                    -d /srv/pgsql/data    -b /usr/bin \\\n"
"                    -D /srv/pgsql/newdata -B ../usr/bin\"\n"
"popd</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/server/databases/postgresql.xml:218
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>pushd $(pwd)/DESTDIR/tmp\n"
"systemctl stop postgresql\n"
"su postgres -c \"../usr/bin/initdb -D /srv/pgsql/newdata\"\n"
"su postgres -c \"../usr/bin/pg_upgrade \\\n"
"                    -d /srv/pgsql/data    -b /usr/bin \\\n"
"                    -D /srv/pgsql/newdata -B ../usr/bin\"\n"
"popd</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/server/databases/postgresql.xml:226
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"At this point, your database files are available in two locations on disk. "
"The old data is located in <filename "
"class=\"directory\">/srv/pgsql/data</filename>, and the new data is in "
"<filename class=\"directory\">/srv/pgsql/newdata</filename>.  Backing up the"
" old database files is recommended before continuing."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/server/databases/postgresql.xml:232
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Next, remove the old database files, and rename the new data directory as "
"the <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem> user:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/server/databases/postgresql.xml:235
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>rm -rf /srv/pgsql/data\n"
"mv /srv/pgsql/newdata /srv/pgsql/data</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/server/databases/postgresql.xml:241
#, xml-text
msgid "Now, as the &root; user:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/server/databases/postgresql.xml:244
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>make install</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/server/databases/postgresql.xml:247
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If you had the optional dependencies installed that are needed to generate "
"the documentation, install it as the &root; user:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/server/databases/postgresql.xml:251
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>make install-docs</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/server/databases/postgresql.xml:254
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If you made any of the <filename class=\"directory\">contrib/</filename> "
"programs, as the <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem> user:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/server/databases/postgresql.xml:258
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>make -C contrib/<replaceable>&lt;SUBDIR-NAME&gt;</replaceable> "
"install</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><tip><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/server/databases/postgresql.xml:262
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If you only intend to use <application>PostgreSQL</application> as a client "
"to connect to a server on another machine, your installation is complete and"
" you should not run the remaining commands."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/server/databases/postgresql.xml:269
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If you have upgraded an existing database, skip the rest of the commands "
"because your database is ready to use. If this is the first time you install"
" <application>PostgreSQL</application>, continue with the initialization."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/server/databases/postgresql.xml:276
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Initialize a database cluster with the following commands issued by the "
"<systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem> user:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/server/databases/postgresql.xml:280
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>install -v -dm700 /srv/pgsql/data &amp;&amp;\n"
"install -v -dm755 /run/postgresql &amp;&amp;\n"
"chown -Rv postgres:postgres /srv/pgsql /run/postgresql</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/server/databases/postgresql.xml:285
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Now, initialize the database as the <systemitem "
"class=\"username\">root</systemitem> user:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/server/databases/postgresql.xml:289
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>su - postgres -c '/usr/bin/initdb -D /srv/pgsql/data'</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/server/databases/postgresql.xml:294
#, xml-text
msgid "Command Explanations"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/server/databases/postgresql.xml:297
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<command>sed -i ...</command>: This sed changes the server socket location "
"from <filename class=\"directory\">/tmp</filename> to <filename "
"class=\"directory\">/run/postgresql</filename>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/server/databases/postgresql.xml:312
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<option>--with-openssl</option>: builds the package with support for "
"<application>OpenSSL</application> encrypted connections."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/server/databases/postgresql.xml:317
#, xml-text
msgid "<option>--with-perl</option>: builds the PL/Perl server-side language."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/server/databases/postgresql.xml:321
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<option>--with-python</option>: builds the PL/Python server-side language."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/server/databases/postgresql.xml:326
#, xml-text
msgid "<option>--with-tcl</option>: builds the PL/Tcl server-side language."
msgstr ""

